{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Unclean by reason of a corpse</b> — there is a paseq between טמא and לנפש, to tell you that there is a distinction among the impure: an individual is displaced, but the congregation is not displaced." "<b>(Or on a journey) far off</b> — רחוקה is in gematria this. The masoretic marking on the heh is as though it were not written." "<b>And they shall keep the Passover to YHWH in the second month</b> — for when they intercalate the year, then Iyar is in place of Nisan, and since on its fifteenth the manna fell, therefore they keep Passover in it. Day one."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "The phrase 'מאסקופה שעל ה\"א נקוד' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. 'מאסקופה' may refer to a masoretic marginal notation or suspension mark on the letter heh; the exact technical sense is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:40.270384126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}